References: <30bceb85ccdffaa64be2221199f7193cb9699a01.camel@groupe-cyllene.com>

This reworks Alexandre Derumier's v2 D-Bus display foundation, with his
original patch and authorship retained. Thanks Alexandre for inviting the
rework. It targets qemu-server a4efa5f9ad2afbf4dea02274ed7a6ff41cdcf0aa.

The VM-wide opt-in proposed here is dbus-display: 1, independent of a
particular console protocol. qemu-server owns one root-private per-VM bus,
creates it before QEMU, and cleans it at VM stop and startup failure.
GPU selection and rendernode stay in vga; audio0 can select driver=dbus.
CPU display permits VNC alongside D-Bus; virtio-gl disables VNC/SPICE.

This series includes the rendernode fix for #4771 and native audio/
qemu-vdagent integration. No QSM package, encoder, WebRTC API, Kyber or RDP
service is required by the common foundation.

Validation: full qemu-server package build, 118 cfg2cmd cases and nine real
bus lifecycle checks. In PVE 9, a second independent D-Bus consumer captured
GL scanouts while the browser console continued decoding frames.

Review questions: top-level dbus-display naming, root-only bus policy,
audio defaults, and common lifecycle placement. The WebRTC consumer and
pve-manager changes are separate series. Optional Markus Frank Venus work
is also separate and not a prerequisite.

Alexandre Derumier (1):
  add D-Bus display support

Dmitry R (5):
  fix #4771: vga: add rendernode option for virtio-gl
  display: integrate the per-VM D-Bus with graphics and audio
  display: protect bus sockets and verify daemon cleanup
  test: cover shared display audio and invalid configurations
  test: run the shared bus lifecycle checks in the test target

